Ladybird drops a tab’s action values when the tab activates another
top-level document, and keeps them across same-document navigations.
Chromium does the same in ExtensionActionRunner::DidFinishNavigation(),
which returns early for a navigation that isn’t in the primary main
frame, hasn’t committed, or is same-document; and Gecko does too, in
ExtensionActions’ handleLocationChange(), which clears the tab’s context
only for a location change from browsing, not for a hash change or
pushState().
